# terra-jupyter-python image

This repo contains the terra-jupyter-python image that is compatible with notebook service in [Terra]("https://app.terra.bio/") called Leonardo. For example, use `us.gcr.io/broad-dsp-gcr-public/terra-jupyter-python:{version}` in terra.

## Image contents

The terra-jupyter-python image extends the [terra-jupyter-base](../terra-jupyter-base) image, supported in this repo.

It installs the packages in [pyproject.toml](./pyproject.toml) (Python 3.13) into the user's conda env
(`$CONDA_ENV_HOME`), which the `python3` notebook kernel runs, including:

- tensorflow
- pandas, numpy, scipy, scikit-learn (with scikit-learn-intelex)
- pymc (replaces pymc3 / theano, which do not support Python 3.13)
- matplotlib, seaborn, plotnine, bokeh, matplotlib-venn
- pysam, biopython, pyvcf3
- pandas-gbq, google-cloud-bigquery-datatransfer

The pyproject.toml is kept in the image at `/etc/terra-docker/pyproject.toml`;
[terra-jupyter-gatk](../terra-jupyter-gatk) reinstalls the same packages from it.

To see the complete contents of this image please see the [Dockerfile](Dockerfile.bak).

## Selecting prior versions of this image

To select an older version this image, you can search the [CHANGELOG.md](./CHANGELOG.md) for a specific package version you need.

Once you find an image version that you want, simply copy and paste the image url from the changelog into the corresponding custom docker field in the Terra notebook runtime widget. 
